<title>USA: Bristol Technology Systems Inc Q3 loss.</title>
<headline>Bristol Technology Systems Inc Q3 loss.</headline>
<dateline>IRVINE, Calif. 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bristol Technology Systems</p>
<p>				  Financial Summary</p>
<p>						1996		     1995</p>
<p>Three Months Ended Sept. 30</p>
<p> Revenues				   $2,119,738  $1,664,260(C)</p>
<p> Net income				    14,566(D)    57,047(C)</p>
<p> Net income per share			  .004(D)     56.99(C)</p>
<p>Weighted average shares of</p>
<p>  common stock outstanding	     3,250,000	 1,001(C)</p>
<p>Nine months Ended Sept. 30</p>
<p> Revenues				 6,137,502(A)   4,426,520(C)</p>
<p> Net income (loss)		    (23,632)(A)(D)   187,873(C)</p>
<p> Net income (loss) per share	  (.008)(A)(D)    187.69(C)</p>
<p>Weighted average shares of</p>
<p>  common stock outstanding	  2,954,355(B)	 1,001(C)</p>
<p>The Company was formed on April 3, 1996 and acquired its wholly-owned subsidiary, Cash Registers, Inc. (CRI) on June 28, 1996.  For comparison purposes, the financial information above includes the historical financial information of CRI as if CRI had always been a subsidiary of the Company.</p>
<p>(A)  Combines the amounts for the Company for the period from inception (April 3, 1996) to September 30, 1996 and CRI for the period from January 1, 1996 to June 28, 1996. Includes revenues and net loss of $4,017,764 and $6,948 for CRI.</p>
<p>(B)  Represents weighted average shares outstanding for Bristol from inception (April 3, 1996) to September 30, 1996.</p>
<p>(C)  Represents amounts for CRI.</p>
<p>(D)  Includes overhead expense for Bristol headquarters.</p>
